<section>
    <div class="container">
        <div class="row">
            <div class="col-lg-8" align="justify">
                <h3><b>Common Release Roadmap Challenges and How to Address Them</b></h3>

                <p>
                    Organizations often struggle to maintain accurate release roadmaps when
                    priorities change frequently or teams work with incomplete information.
                    Identifying common challenges early helps product teams create more
                    reliable and actionable release plans.
                </p>

                <h5><b>Unclear Release Priorities</b></h5>
                <p>
                    When every feature is treated as a priority, teams may struggle to
                    determine what should be delivered first. A value-based prioritization
                    approach helps identify the releases that have the greatest strategic
                    and customer impact.
                </p>

                <h5><b>Unrealistic Delivery Commitments</b></h5>
                <p>
                    Roadmaps can become unreliable when delivery dates are established
                    without considering development complexity, testing, dependencies, or
                    team capacity. Release planning should use realistic estimates and
                    clearly communicate assumptions.
                </p>

                <h5><b>Changing Business Requirements</b></h5>
                <p>
                    Market conditions, customer expectations, and business strategies can
                    change during product development. A flexible roadmap allows teams to
                    adjust priorities without losing sight of long-term product objectives.
                </p>

                <h5><b>Poor Cross-Team Communication</b></h5>
                <p>
                    Engineering, product, marketing, sales, and support teams may have
                    different expectations about upcoming releases. Regular roadmap reviews
                    and transparent communication help maintain alignment.
                </p>

                <h5><b>Unmanaged Dependencies</b></h5>
                <p>
                    Dependencies between teams, systems, integrations, and vendors can
                    introduce unexpected delays. Mapping dependencies during roadmap
                    planning allows teams to identify potential blockers earlier.
                </p>

                <h5><b>Lack of Post-Release Evaluation</b></h5>
                <p>
                    A release roadmap should not end when a feature is deployed. Reviewing
                    adoption, customer feedback, performance, and business results helps
                    teams understand whether releases achieved their intended objectives.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="col-lg-4 text-center">
                @* Add the relevant release planning image here when available. *@
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section>
