<section>
    <div class="container">
        <div class="row">
            <div class="col-lg-8" align="justify">
                <h3><b>Release Readiness and Stakeholder Communication</b></h3>

                <p>
                    Before a release is delivered, teams should confirm that the product,
                    technology, documentation, support processes, and business teams are
                    ready. A release roadmap should provide visibility into readiness
                    activities and clearly communicate responsibilities across teams.
                </p>

                <h5><b>Product and Engineering Readiness</b></h5>
                <p>
                    Confirm that planned features have completed development and meet the
                    defined acceptance criteria. Technical reviews, integration checks,
                    security validation, and performance testing should be completed where
                    applicable.
                </p>

                <h5><b>Quality Assurance</b></h5>
                <p>
                    Testing should validate functionality, usability, compatibility, and
                    reliability before the release reaches customers. Critical defects
                    should be resolved or formally assessed before deployment.
                </p>

                <h5><b>Business and Operational Readiness</b></h5>
                <p>
                    Marketing, sales, customer support, operations, and other relevant teams
                    should understand what is changing and how the release affects
                    customers and internal processes.
                </p>

                <h5><b>Release Communication</b></h5>
                <p>
                    Clear communication ensures that stakeholders know the release scope,
                    expected date, key changes, known limitations, and actions required
                    before launch.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="col-lg-4 text-center">
                @* Add the relevant release readiness image here when available. *@
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

